    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fb50f7b3-6bec-5105-8228-becc03ae11b2",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,F=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,G=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $EF=FE={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $EG=GE={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $G={E}^{-1}$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $EF=FE={I}_{2}.$ Computing $EF$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EF & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $FE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FE & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $EG=GE={I}_{2}.$ Computing $EG$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EG & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & 6 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $G\\ne {E}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d6e11f4d-3ec0-512e-9afe-7f1894513424",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
