      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n\nII. $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n\nIII. $B={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $B={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\".",
