    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5d05bcca-7b20-517c-a0f3-e5e624a69ec8",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $B={A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & -1 \\\\ \u2217 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
