    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6bc69960-8a89-531f-a264-4183d08ba6f3",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $AB = BA = I_{2}$\n2. $AC = CA = I_{2}$\n3. $B = A^{-1}$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each pair multiplies to $I_2$.\n\nComputing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d45e93c1-a675-5a24-9467-5cc501c49419",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
