    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "da26ab4b-7794-5924-ad25-d72a1701f8a8",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $BC=CB={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $BD=DB={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $D={B}^{-1}$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- First, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{2}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ -4 & \u2217\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $BD=DB={I}_{2}.$ Computing $BD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $D={B}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "037bce32-ee66-5263-88bc-40b972688c56",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "c78f21ad-1952-578d-80ef-65f6e5f0656c",
